# core-api environment.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `core/config.py` calls load_dotenv(), so a `.env` in the repository root is read
# automatically. Values below are the defaults the code applies when a variable is
# absent -- copying this file unchanged reproduces default behaviour, except for the
# few variables marked REQUIRED, which have no default and raise on startup.
#
# If you are updating an existing .env written before the spread-pattern redesign, read
# the MIGRATING section at the bottom: several variables were deleted and four changed
# meaning. Stale entries are not warned about; they are silently obeyed or ignored.


# --- required -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# No default. The app raises KeyError at import time if these are unset.

JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Vertex AI, read directly by core/analysis/genai.py. Needs Application Default
# Credentials as well (`gcloud auth application-default login`), which is separate
# from these values.
GEMINI_PROJECT=pas-development-1
GEMINI_LOCATION=global
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite


# --- general ------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Prefix for external links pointing back at this service. Locally that is normally
# http://localhost:8000; deployed it is the public host.
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# "dev" relaxes production-only behaviour. Anything else means production.
DEVELOPMENT_MODE=dev

# GCS bucket holding video content.
VIDEO_STORAGE_BUCKET_NAME=


# --- database -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# These match the pas-postgres service in compose.yaml. Keep the two in step.
DATABASE_HOST=localhost
DATABASE_PORT=5432
DATABASE_USER=pas
DATABASE_PASSWORD=s3cret
DATABASE_NAME=pas


# --- auth ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# JSON array, parsed with json.loads. Machine-to-machine keys for the X-API-TOKEN
# header. Must be valid JSON: ["key1","key2"], not a bare comma-separated list.
API_KEYS=[]


# --- email --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mailgun is used when configured; SMTP is the fallback. Both may be left empty in
# local development, in which case no mail is sent.

EMAIL_FROM=no-reply@mail.prebunking.efcsn.com
MAILGUN_DOMAIN=
MAILGUN_API_KEY=

SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=
SMTP_USERNAME=
SMTP_PASSWORD=


# --- narratives service -------------------------------------------------------------
# No default: unset leaves these None and calls to the service fail at call time.

NARRATIVES_BASE_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8001
NARRATIVES_API_KEY=


# --- virality and spread-pattern tuning -----------------------------------------------
#
# Every default below is the production value, so you only need these lines if you are
# deliberately retuning. Setting them to anything else changes how narratives are
# classified. See docs/narrative-spread-pattern-redesign.md for the reasoning.
#
# NOTHING VALIDATES THESE AT RUNTIME. The two sum-to-1 rules and the one ordering
# constraint are conventions the code assumes, not checks it performs. A wrong value
# produces a running service with quietly wrong scores.

# Raw engagement weighting, applied before any ranking.
VIRALITY_SCORE_LIKES_WEIGHT=1
VIRALITY_SCORE_COMMENTS_WEIGHT=5

# Composite virality -- the VIRALITY-STATE axis: how viral a narrative already is.
# MUST SUM TO 1. Reach leads: it is the only term that answers "how big is this",
# because engagement_score is a per-view ratio and therefore size-neutral. Engagement
# is the tiebreak between narratives of comparable size, not the headline.
COMPOSITE_ENGAGEMENT_WEIGHT=0.375
COMPOSITE_REACH_WEIGHT=0.625

# Acceleration rate -- the CHANGE-IN-VIRALITY axis: speed of distribution.
# MUST SUM TO 1, and ACCELERATION_ENGAGEMENT_WEIGHT MUST STAY BELOW
# ACCELERATION_VIEWS_WEIGHT. Engagement change is a modifier on distribution speed and
# must not be able to overturn it: if it can, a narrative whose views grew while its
# engagement ratio dipped scores a negative rate and is floored to zero.
ACCELERATION_ENGAGEMENT_WEIGHT=0.10
ACCELERATION_VIDEO_VOLUME_WEIGHT=0.35
ACCELERATION_VIEWS_WEIGHT=0.55

# Spread-pattern cut points, as PERCENT_RANK within each narrative's own cohort -- never
# raw values, so each threshold means a knowable fraction of the cohort and stays
# self-calibrating as scraper coverage drifts.
#
# The four labels are RECTANGLES on the percentile plane, not quadrants, which is why
# there are six thresholds rather than two, and why the bottom-left (small AND flat) is
# a no-badge region. Resulting labels: viral, early_surge, consolidated, trending, or
# NULL. See NarrativeService._classify for evaluation order.
SPREAD_COMPOSITE_LO=0.40   # early_surge ceiling / trending floor
SPREAD_COMPOSITE_MID=0.50  # consolidated floor
SPREAD_COMPOSITE_HI=0.80   # viral floor
SPREAD_ACCEL_LO=0.40       # consolidated ceiling / trending floor
SPREAD_ACCEL_MID=0.50      # early_surge floor
SPREAD_ACCEL_HI=0.80       # viral floor


# ====================================================================================
# MIGRATING AN OLDER .env
# ====================================================================================
#
# The spread-pattern redesign renamed the output (alert level -> spread pattern) and
# reworked the tuning surface. Infrastructure variables -- database, auth, email,
# narratives, Gemini -- are untouched; carry them across as they are.
#
# Only the virality block changed, in three ways.
#
#
# 1. DELETE these lines. They are read by nothing and will be ignored, but leaving
#    them implies a control that no longer exists:
#
#      COMPOSITE_VELOCITY_WEIGHT              velocity is gone from the state axis
#                                             entirely -- a growth term there
#                                             double-counted what the acceleration axis
#                                             exists to measure
#      COMPOSITE_PERCENTILE_VIRAL             replaced, see 2
#      COMPOSITE_PERCENTILE_WATCH_MIN         replaced, see 2
#      COMPOSITE_PERCENTILE_EARLY_SURGE_MAX   replaced, see 2
#      ACCELERATION_PERCENTILE_SURGE          replaced, see 2
#      ACCELERATION_PERCENTILE_WATCH_MIN      replaced, see 2
#      ACCELERATION_CHANGE_CAP                no longer applied
#      VIRALITY_SCORE_REACH_CAP_LIMIT         the reach cap is gone; downstream reads
#                                             PERCENT_RANK, which a monotonic transform
#                                             cannot move, while the clip tied the
#                                             largest narratives into one block at the
#                                             exact top of the axis that viral and
#                                             consolidated are read from
#
#
# 2. The five *_PERCENTILE_* variables became the six SPREAD_* thresholds above.
#
#    THIS IS NOT A RENAME -- DO NOT CARRY THE OLD NUMBERS ACROSS. The old knobs were
#    one threshold per label on a two-quadrant reading; the new ones are the grid
#    boundaries of four rectangles, which is why one set of six now serves all labels.
#    A value that meant "viral starts at the 95th percentile" has no equivalent slot.
#    Start from the defaults above and retune from there if you need to.
#
#
# 3. These four kept their names but changed meaning. IF YOUR .env SETS THEM
#    EXPLICITLY, UPDATE THE VALUES -- an old .env silently overrides the new defaults
#    and keeps computing the old classification with the new code:
#
#                                        old     new
#      COMPOSITE_ENGAGEMENT_WEIGHT       0.50    0.375
#      COMPOSITE_REACH_WEIGHT            0.30    0.625
#      ACCELERATION_VIEWS_WEIGHT         0.25    0.55
#      ACCELERATION_ENGAGEMENT_WEIGHT    0.40    0.10
#      ACCELERATION_VIDEO_VOLUME_WEIGHT  0.35    0.35   (unchanged)
#
#    The composite pair is the redesign's substance: reach now leads instead of
#    engagement. The magnitudes are a free choice; the ordering is not.
#
#    Note the arithmetic trap. The old composite weights summed to 1 only with
#    velocity's 0.20 included. Keeping engagement=0.50 and reach=0.30 after deleting
#    COMPOSITE_VELOCITY_WEIGHT leaves a sum of 0.80, and nothing will tell you.
#
#    On the acceleration side the old 0.40/0.35/0.25 violated the ordering constraint
#    above. Measured against 2026-07-16 (n=2237), that erased 679 genuine growers to a
#    zero rate; the current weights erase 43.
#
#
# After changing any of these, recompute the derived tables -- the stored spread patterns
# were classified under the old configuration and are not updated in place:
#
#   .venv/bin/python -m core.cli run-narrative-analysis-indicators-pipeline
#
# Neither narrative_virality_scores nor narrative_analysis_indicators has a unique key,
# so each run STACKS rows rather than replacing them. narratives.spread_pattern itself is
# overwritten. For a clean recompute locally, reset the seed data first.
